WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.433 --> 00:00:02.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
-If you need
to laugh this weekend,

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:03.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
tune in to SNL.
It is going remote.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:05.005 line:92%
-"Saturday Night Live" returns

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:07.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
with an all-new episode
from home.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.241 line:92%
-It's gonna be so fascinating

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:09.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
to see them
in their element at home.

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:13.413 size:84% position:42%
-I can't wait to see
how they pull that off.

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:15.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Initially, I was like,
"Oh, man!

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.384 size:75% position:38% line:92%
This is gonna suck!"

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:20.420 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughing ]

00:00:24.591 --> 00:00:26.593 line:92%
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:27.660 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I'm Daniel Craig.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
This has been
"Saturday Night Live."

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:31.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you.
Thank you. Thank you.

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:34.934 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.169 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That last show...

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:37.804 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Rewinding ]

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:41.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
it didn't feel like
we wouldn't be coming back.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:42.442 size:84% position:42% line:92%
There was no indication

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:47.447
that that would kind of be
our live show season finale.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:50.650
-I think I got an email
that was just sent to everybody

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:53.186
and they were like, "Hey,
we're gonna do it at home now."

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:55.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I remember being
a little perplexed

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:57.891 line:92%
as to how we would do it.

00:00:57.891 --> 00:00:59.225 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-"SNL" is so much chaos.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:01.661
The one sort of grounding force
we have is the audience.

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:05.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We do a multicam
live sketch show.

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:07.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
So the we feed off
of the studio audience.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The suspect, described
as a white male --

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:10.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Whew!
-Love it!

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:12.939 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:14.340 line:92%
-The show's always been at 8H.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.409 line:92%
We've always done it at 30 Rock.

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:20.346
-But, if everyone else is in,
I'm in and, I mean, I'm excited

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:21.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause what else am I doing?
I'm home.

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:24.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This equipment would arrive
at our house.

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:25.852 line:92%
We'd be like, "What is this?

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:29.923
I guess there's a sketch
involving a greenscreen."

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:31.958 line:92%
So, now, we have a greenscreen,

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:34.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
-For the first show.
we did a Zoom table read.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I hope you guys enjoy
our table read here

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:39.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we'll see what we
come up with on Saturday.

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:40.700 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
This is crazy.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And one of the sketches
we read at the table

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:44.838 size:75% position:38% line:92%
was the dating show.

00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:47.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hello and welcome
to "How Low Will You Go?"

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:51.811
-The most surreal moment --
there was a dating show.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:56.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got up and stood on the side
of my little computer area,

00:01:56.015 --> 00:02:00.587
waiting for my cue as they were
doing the sketch on Zoom

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:03.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it feels kind of like
the normal show.

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:04.691 line:92%
You're waiting for your cue.

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:07.293 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Hello-o-o, ladies!

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:09.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I just remember having
a distinct moment,

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:12.732
thinking like,
"I will remember this forever."

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:15.735
-You're setting up a ring light
and a greenscreen

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:17.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
and all these things
that you don't usually do.

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:19.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, then, by the time
you're shooting the thing,

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:21.808 size:88% position:44% line:92%
you're just overwhelmed.

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:24.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was also crazy because,
our first show back,

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:26.012 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Hal Willner died.

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:28.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just like can't picture
working on a sketch

00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:29.582 size:84% position:42% line:92%
without talking to him.

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:31.417 size:81% position:41% line:92%
It was very difficult.

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:32.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This was challenging.
-It was hard,

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:35.755
but we were in it together,
and that was really nice.

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:40.160 line:92%
-For the SoulCycle sketch,

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
my next door neighbors
yelled lines

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:45.031 size:88% position:44% line:92%
in response to my lines.

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:47.867
-It's crazy to think that people
could be watching this

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:49.669 line:92%
anywhere from Los Angeles

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:51.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
to California.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:55.241
I heard my neighbor say,
"Los Angeles is in California."

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:57.777
Like they didn't get that
I was shooting a sketch.

00:02:57.777 --> 00:02:58.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Knocking ]
I knocked on their door.

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:00.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was just like,
"We're shooting this thing."

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:03.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
I apologize.
It won't happen again.

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:04.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
But maybe it will happen
again in two weeks."

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:07.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
The first thing I did was
I did the Drake song

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:09.556 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and the Andre 2000 song.

00:03:09.556 --> 00:03:11.024 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was super weird.

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:13.826
We would go outside and dance
in the middle of the street

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:15.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then like
my neighbor would come

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:18.798 size:81% position:41%
and get like his mail
and just like look up.

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:22.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'd be like,
[ Laughing ] "SNL at Home."

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:24.103 line:92%
-♪ I'm stuck in the core ♪

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:25.305 size:78% position:39% line:92%
♪ Got nothin' to do ♪

00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:27.273 size:81% position:41%
-I had this other song
that I was workin' on,

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:29.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I just, on a whim,
sent to Sandler

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:30.743 line:92%
and he ended up liking it

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:33.613
and then he was just like,
"I'm gonna do a verse on this,"

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:35.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was like, "Holy [bleep]
This is crazy."

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:38.818
♪ I'm so [bleep] bored,
I'm doin' songs with me ♪

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:41.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
♪ Stuck with my fam,
I can't get out ♪

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:44.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And that is, by far,
my favorite like SNL moment

00:03:44.424 --> 00:03:46.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
like that I've ever had,
for sure.

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:48.761 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-♪ And crazy ♪

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:51.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It got better
as the weeks went on.

00:03:51.698 --> 00:03:53.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Paul?
-Mandy?

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:54.667 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah! Mandy!

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:58.571
-I guess, slowly, things just
stopped being as overwhelming.

00:03:58.571 --> 00:03:59.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then, the second one,
you know,

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:01.975
we cranked it up a notch
because, now, we had time

00:04:01.975 --> 00:04:04.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
to send wigs out,
and send costumes

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:06.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was obvious
in that second episode.

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:07.714 line:92%
-I guess one of the best parts

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:10.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
was how our families
got involved.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.718 size:81% position:41% line:92%
My seven-year-old son,

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:13.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
he would be
in our read-throughs.

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:15.021 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Indistinct ]

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:17.357 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-It's hard on them, too.

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:19.392 line:92%
-Like this bitch knows anything.

00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:21.461 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.461 --> 00:04:23.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We worked on this dad
prank sketch.

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:25.064 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-So I have a...

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:26.466 size:75% position:38% line:92%
[ Electronic voice ]

00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:28.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Brandon!
-[ Electronic voice ]

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:30.336 line:92%
-I wrote him a thank you.

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:31.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
Right now, it's just
kind of annoying

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:33.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
to have to go up
and shoot and stuff, but,

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:37.810
when you're older, I think
you'll think it's pretty cool

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:40.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you got to be a part
of this show.

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:45.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Watchin' my daughter
watch herself

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:48.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
in my intro on the show,
she was just beaming.

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:50.590 line:92%
She just couldn't stop smiling,

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:52.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
that, I mean, I could've
cried, watchin' that.

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:53.726 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Can you say bye-bye?

00:04:53.726 --> 00:04:55.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Bye-bye.
-Bye-bye!

00:04:55.161 --> 00:04:58.998
To see what you do immediately
impact your child like that,

00:04:58.998 --> 00:05:00.366 line:92%
that was a very touching moment.

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:02.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
-At-home episodes
sort of felt like

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:03.503 size:84% position:42% line:92%
we got a job to do here

00:05:03.503 --> 00:05:05.705
and it just sort of felt
like an experimental thing.

00:05:05.705 --> 00:05:07.874 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Especially when Brad Pitt
said it, like "Live..."

00:05:07.874 --> 00:05:10.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...kinda,
from all across America,

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:11.544 size:75% position:38% line:92%
it's Saturday night.

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:12.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like, "Okay,
we're gettin' a glimpse

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:15.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
into an invincibility
with the show."

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:17.517 size:78% position:39%
Like whether we do it
at 30 Rock or not,

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:18.851 line:92%
I think we can figure out a way

00:05:18.851 --> 00:05:20.119 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
to get it done.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:25.625 line:92%
-For the "Dreams" sketch,

00:05:25.625 --> 00:05:27.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't know what
everyone else was doing.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I had been reading an article
about COVID dreams

00:05:29.696 --> 00:05:31.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
and how intense
they were for people

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:33.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'd had some myself,
so I started to think

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:37.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
like what would it be like
to see the dreams of the cast,

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:38.504 line:92%
what they miss and, you know,

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:40.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
maybe what we all
sort of miss about New York?

00:05:40.973 --> 00:05:44.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The director, Paul Briganti,
directed over Zoom.

00:05:44.544 --> 00:05:46.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Alright.
And action.

00:05:46.179 --> 00:05:47.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We did like
a read-through of it.

00:05:47.447 --> 00:05:49.449 line:92%
After we finished reading it,

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:50.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
all of us just looked
at each other's

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:54.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
little tiles on Zoom
and we were like silent.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:57.457
And then I remember breaking
the silence by being like...

00:05:57.457 --> 00:05:59.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
I hope everyone
has a good summer.

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:00.660 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:02.095 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah!

00:06:02.095 --> 00:06:06.632
-Seeing the city and us being
digitally put into the city

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:10.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
was kinda bittersweet and sad,
but, at the same time,

00:06:10.636 --> 00:06:13.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
uplifting,
seeing us all together again.

00:06:13.172 --> 00:06:16.042
-I guess we just never thought
that we would get to a point

00:06:16.042 --> 00:06:18.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
where we wouldn't be able
to have New York.

00:06:18.678 --> 00:06:20.446 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Walk in Times Square,

00:06:20.446 --> 00:06:22.915
be bumped into on Fifth Avenue,
or any of that.

00:06:22.915 --> 00:06:24.217 size:81% position:41% line:92%
It was very emotional.

00:06:25.585 --> 00:06:27.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Those shows were
a nice reminder

00:06:27.553 --> 00:06:29.756
that this is still possible,
that it was still possible

00:06:29.756 --> 00:06:31.691 align:start size:94% position:6%
to sort of be there
for each other,

00:06:31.691 --> 00:06:33.793 line:92%
even though we were so separate.

00:06:33.793 --> 00:06:36.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Getting to watch that episode
from the comfort of my home

00:06:36.562 --> 00:06:39.265
in New York made me feel
so connected to the city.

00:06:39.265 --> 00:06:42.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Coming off the elevator
Saturday night

00:06:42.068 --> 00:06:44.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
and seeing a neighbor
who was like,

00:06:44.303 --> 00:06:45.805 line:92%
"Are you gonna watch your show?"

00:06:45.805 --> 00:06:47.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughing ]
I was like,

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Yeah.
Are you gonna watch it?"

00:06:49.609 --> 00:06:52.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm waiting for us to be able
to get back in 30 Rock.

00:06:52.979 --> 00:06:55.915
Oh, man. I wish I could get
a good night's hug right now.

00:06:55.915 --> 00:06:57.650
-I can't wait to go back.
I can't wait to go back

00:06:57.650 --> 00:06:58.651 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and see everybody.

00:06:58.651 --> 00:06:59.786 line:92%
-I'm really like grateful

00:06:59.786 --> 00:07:01.521 line:92%
that we had those three shows.

00:07:01.521 --> 00:07:03.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
I won't forget
and I'm like appreciative

00:07:03.723 --> 00:07:06.726 align:start size:94% position:6%
to have been part of it.
-Yay! That was great.

00:07:06.726 --> 00:07:08.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yay!
[ Laughter ]

00:07:08.461 --> 00:07:10.062 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Static crackles ]

00:07:10.062 --> 00:07:12.732 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-What I wanna say is

00:07:12.732 --> 00:07:14.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
we'll get through
this thing together,

00:07:14.167 --> 00:07:16.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
but we'll also come
out on the other side

00:07:16.135 --> 00:07:18.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
with a little more compassion
and appreciation

00:07:18.371 --> 00:07:21.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
for our world
that we live in, you know?

00:07:21.107 --> 00:07:23.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
Show some more love
to each other,

00:07:23.209 --> 00:07:25.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
show some more
love to our planet.

00:07:25.845 --> 00:07:27.280 line:92%
That's all I can hope for.

